You are incorrect, as usual. 

Dunce caps do not have a special case in the object-creation
function; as such, they have the same chance of being blessed or cursed
as any other piece of armor not explicitly called out.  The four items
which are called out are the fumble boots, levitation boots, helm of
opposite alignment, and gauntlets of fumbling.  These four items have a
90% chance of being generated cursed.

All other armor pieces, including the dunce cap, have a small chance of
being cursed (approximately 5%) and a small chance of being blessed
(slightly more than 5%).

What this means is that it is not possible to reliably use your pet to
distinguish a dunce cap from a cornuthaum, as 95% of the time the dunce
cap will be uncursed or blessed and thus not objectionable to the pet.

